    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84926" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολῠ-κέφᾰλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>many-headed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					588c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφιστής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Sph.</u>
					240c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				769b27
			</span></i>; of plants, interpol. in <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.152
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. στρέβλα</span> (with allusion
			to <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
			</span></i>l.c.) <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>4 Ma.</u>
				7.14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος π.,</span> a celebrated air
			on the flute, so called from its expressing <i>the hissing of the
				serpents round the Gorgon's head,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1133d
			</span></i>.</div>
